---
// Page 01: four problems, shown one at a time, each with a sketch and what changes with the skills.
---

<bm-tabs class="ptabs not-content">
  <div role="tablist" aria-label="Problems">
    <button role="tab" type="button" id="p-tab-1" aria-controls="p-panel-1" aria-selected="true">Agents go deep before they go wide.</button>
    <button role="tab" type="button" id="p-tab-2" aria-controls="p-panel-2" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Behavior changes get drawn into implementation details.</button>
    <button role="tab" type="button" id="p-tab-3" aria-controls="p-panel-3" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Agents reinvent concepts between sessions.</button>
    <button role="tab" type="button" id="p-tab-4" aria-controls="p-panel-4" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">The code's structure drifts from your mental model.</button>
  </div>

  <div class="ppanel" role="tabpanel" id="p-panel-1" aria-labelledby="p-tab-1">
    <p>Ask for a change and an agent dives into the first part it sees, down to schemas and error messages, while the rest of the change is still unclear.</p>
    <div class="sk" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="sk-root">Pay with gift cards</div>
      <div class="sk-row">
        <div class="sk-col">
          <div class="sk-node">Place order</div>
          <div class="sk-deep">gift_cards table</div>
          <div class="sk-deep">POST /orders</div>
          <div class="sk-deep">error codes</div>
        </div>
        <div class="sk-col"><div class="sk-node off">Balance?</div></div>
        <div class="sk-col"><div class="sk-node off">Charges?</div></div>
        <div class="sk-col"><div class="sk-node off">Mobile app?</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="skcap">Three levels down on one part. The other three are still open.</p>
    <p class="pfix"><span class="klab">With the skills</span>Every behavior change is laid out first. The details wait until the whole change is agreed.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="ppanel" role="tabpanel" id="p-panel-2" aria-labelledby="p-tab-2" hidden>
    <p>You want to agree on what people will be able to do. The conversation turns to tables, endpoints and files before you have.</p>
    <div class="sk sk-talk" aria-hidden="true">
      <p><span class="who">You</span>Shoppers should be able to pay with gift cards.</p>
      <p class="ag" style="--i: 1"><span class="who">Agent</span>I'll add a <code>gift_cards</code> table with a balance column.</p>
      <p class="ag" style="--i: 2"><span class="who">Agent</span>Then a <code>POST /gift-cards/redeem</code> endpoint.</p>
      <p class="ag" style="--i: 3"><span class="who">Agent</span>And split the amount in <code>charge.ts</code>.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="skcap">What shoppers can do was never agreed. The talk moved to how.</p>
    <p class="pfix"><span class="klab">With the skills</span>Each change is stated as what changes for the people using the system, marked against the map, and you confirm it before any code.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="ppanel" role="tabpanel" id="p-panel-3" aria-labelledby="p-tab-3" hidden>
    <p>One session says gift card, the next says voucher, the one after that adds a prepaid balance. Nothing holds the names you agreed on.</p>
    <div class="sk sk-sessions" aria-hidden="true">
      <div><span class="klab">Session 1</span><span class="chip2">Gift card</span></div>
      <div><span class="klab">Session 2</span><span class="chip2">Voucher</span></div>
      <div><span class="klab">Session 3</span><span class="chip2">Prepaid balance</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="skcap">One concept, three names.</p>
    <p class="pfix"><span class="klab">With the skills</span>You settle the names when you review the map. Every change is then planned in those names, and fuzzy words get questioned.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="ppanel" role="tabpanel" id="p-panel-4" aria-labelledby="p-tab-4" hidden>
    <p>The parts you have in mind stop lining up with the folders and services in the code, and nobody notices until a change gets hard.</p>
    <div class="sk" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg class="sk-svg" viewBox="0 0 380 140">
        <text class="m-k" x="0" y="12">IN YOUR HEAD</text>
        <text class="m-k" x="240" y="12">IN THE CODE</text>
        <path class="m-line" d="M121 47 C180 47 180 38 240 38"></path>
        <path class="m-line" d="M121 47 C180 47 180 76 240 76"></path>
        <path class="m-line" d="M121 47 C180 47 180 114 240 114"></path>
        <path class="m-line" d="M121 107 C180 107 180 76 240 76"></path>
        <path class="m-line" d="M121 107 C180 107 180 114 240 114"></path>
        <rect class="m-hi" x="0.5" y="32" width="120" height="30" rx="4"></rect>
        <text class="m-n" x="12" y="51">Storefront</text>
        <rect class="m-hi" x="0.5" y="92" width="120" height="30" rx="4"></rect>
        <text class="m-n" x="12" y="111">Payments</text>
        <rect class="m-in" x="240" y="24" width="139" height="28" rx="4"></rect>
        <text class="m-c" x="252" y="42">src/shop/</text>
        <rect class="m-in" x="240" y="62" width="139" height="28" rx="4"></rect>
        <text class="m-c" x="252" y="80">src/checkout/</text>
        <rect class="m-in" x="240" y="100" width="139" height="28" rx="4"></rect>
        <text class="m-c" x="252" y="118">src/billing/</text>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <p class="skcap">Two parts in your head, three folders in the code, and no clean line between them.</p>
    <p class="pfix"><span class="klab">With the skills</span>The map cites the code behind each boundary. Updating it shows what changed in the code since the last review.</p>
  </div>
</bm-tabs>

<script>
  // Shows one panel at a time. Arrow keys move between tabs, as in any tab list.
  class Tabs extends HTMLElement {
    connectedCallback() {
      const tabs = [...this.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[role="tab"]')];
      const select = (tab: HTMLButtonElement) => {
        for (const t of tabs) {
          const on = t === tab;
          t.setAttribute("aria-selected", String(on));
          t.tabIndex = on ? 0 : -1;
          const panel = this.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`#${t.getAttribute("aria-controls")}`);
          if (panel) panel.hidden = !on;
        }
      };
      for (const [i, tab] of tabs.entries()) {
        tab.addEventListener("click", () => select(tab));
        tab.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
          const step = { ArrowDown: 1, ArrowRight: 1, ArrowUp: -1, ArrowLeft: -1 }[e.key];
          if (!step) return;
          e.preventDefault();
          const next = tabs[(i + step + tabs.length) % tabs.length];
          select(next);
          next.focus();
        });
      }
    }
  }
  customElements.define("bm-tabs", Tabs);
</script>

<style>
  .ptabs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 210px minmax(0, 1fr);
    margin-top: 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--bm-line);
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  [role="tablist"] {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--bm-line);
    background: var(--bm-panel);
  }
  [role="tab"] {
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border: 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bm-line);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--bm-fg3);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.4;
    text-align: left;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  [role="tab"]:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  [role="tab"][aria-selected="true"] {
    color: var(--bm-fg);
    background: var(--bm-bg);
    box-shadow: inset 2px 0 0 var(--bm-fg);
  }
  .ppanel {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 18px 20px;
  }
  .ppanel[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  .ppanel > p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--bm-fg2);
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .ppanel .skcap {
    margin-top: -6px;
    color: var(--bm-fg3);
    font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .ppanel .pfix {
    padding-top: 12px;
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--bm-line2);
    color: var(--bm-fg);
    font-size: 13.5px;
  }
  .klab {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    color: var(--bm-fg3);
    font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .sk {
    padding: 14px;
    border: 1px solid var(--bm-line);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--bm-panel);
  }
  .sk-root {
    width: max-content;
    max-width: 100%;
    margin: 0 auto 12px;
    padding: 3px 10px;
    border: 1px solid var(--bm-fg3);
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--bm-bg);
    color: var(--bm-fg);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .sk-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.8fr) repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .sk-col {
    display: grid;
    gap: 4px;
    align-content: start;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .sk-node {
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: 3px 6px;
    border: 1px solid var(--bm-fg3);
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--bm-bg);
    color: var(--bm-fg);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    text-align: center;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .sk-node.off {
    border-style: dashed;
    border-color: var(--bm-line2);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--bm-fg4);
  }
  .sk-deep {
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-left: 10px;
    padding: 2px 0 2px 8px;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--bm-fg3);
    color: var(--bm-fg);
    font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .sk-talk p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--bm-fg);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .sk-talk .ag {
    margin-top: 6px;
    margin-left: calc(var(--i) * 18px);
    color: var(--bm-fg2);
  }
  .sk-talk .who {
    margin-right: 8px;
    color: var(--bm-fg3);
    font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .sk-talk code {
    color: var(--bm-fg);
    font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
  }
  .sk-sessions {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .sk-sessions > div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 8px 10px;
    border: 1px solid var(--bm-line2);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--bm-bg);
  }
  .chip2 {
    justify-self: start;
    padding: 1px 9px;
    border: 1px dashed var(--bm-fg3);
    border-radius: 10px;
    color: var(--bm-fg);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .sk-svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 420px;
    height: auto;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .m-k {
    fill: var(--bm-fg3);
    font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 8.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }
  .m-n {
    fill: var(--bm-fg);
    font-family: var(--__sl-font);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .m-c {
    fill: var(--bm-fg2);
    font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
  }
  .m-line {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--bm-fg4);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  .m-hi {
    fill: var(--bm-bg);
    stroke: var(--bm-fg3);
    stroke-width: 1.2;
  }
  .m-in {
    fill: var(--bm-panel);
    stroke: var(--bm-line2);
    stroke-width: 1;
  }
  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .ptabs {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
    [role="tablist"] {
      border-right: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bm-line);
    }
    .sk-row {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
    .sk-sessions {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
